<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Via Toledo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1536">1536</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Via <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toledo</a> is one of the main streets of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a>, laid out in 1536 by the Spanish viceroy Pedro de Toledo along the line of the old western walls. Running for over a kilometre from Piazza <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dante-alighieri">Dante</a> towards the royal palace, it became the city's principal thoroughfare, lined with noble palaces, while the grid of the Spanish Quarters was built beside it to house troops.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/via-toledo.jpg" alt="Via Toledo" width="320" height="428" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Napoli_-_Toledo_aka_Via_Roma.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Pedro de Toledo, viceroy from 1532 to 1553, strengthened royal justice and remodelled the capital, laying out the <b>Via Toledo</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-naples">Kingdom of Naples · Governance &amp; Law</a></li></ul></section>
